  "result": "Here's the draft:\n\n```markdown\n## Carriers\n\nEach carrier is its own module in `shop/carriers/` (20 in all, `acme.py` through\n`tundra.py`). Each one is registered by name in `shop/carriers/__init__.py`, and\nyou look one up with `carriers.get(\"acme\")`.\n\nEvery carrier module defines `BASE_RATE`, a flat charge in cents. `rate(weight, zone)`\nadds a per-weight charge to it and multiplies the total by a zone factor.\n\nAll carriers take weight in kilograms except **Maple** (`maple.py`), which takes\ngrams (`PER_GRAMS`, max 30000 g). Convert to grams before you call Maple's `rate()`.\n```\n\nThat's about 80 words. I checked the details against the code: all 20 modules define `BASE_RATE`, and only `maple.py` uses grams. I didn't check that every carrier uses the same zone names, so the draft doesn't list them.\n\nI haven't changed `README.md`. Tell me if you want it added there, under the existing intro line.",
